summary:
  What the widget writes down about a failed cast carries the helper's own
  words after the fields.

history:
  A failed cast leaves one line in the journal now, so that the next report
  can say which action a device refused and with which code. Journals get
  pasted into reports, and a station's address can hold a listener's token.
  The line is made of the fields the helper named, each of which may hold
  only what such a field holds; the words behind them can be anything a
  device chose to say.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
          return { "kind": "refused", "log": f.action + " refused, UPnP " + f.upnp };

replace:
          return { "kind": "refused", "log": f.action + " refused, UPnP " + f.upnp + " " + out };

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_the_address_is_never_in_what_is_written_down.
